From: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 16:43:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] smb: server: remove unused DES crypto header
References: bsc#1258210
Patch-mainline: 6.18.52
Git-commit: c5e640fe346177372ff4a51a45b01fcd48c29207

[ Upstream commit c5e640fe346177372ff4a51a45b01fcd48c29207 ]

The DES crypto header is no longer used after the removal of NTLMv1
authentication. Remove it now that the server no longer selects
CRYPTO_LIB_DES.

Fixes: ce812992f239 ("ksmbd: remove NTLMv1 authentication")
Signed-off-by: Namjae Jeon <linkinjeon@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Sasha Levin <sashal@kernel.org>
Signed-off-by: Robert Frohl <rfrohl@suse.com>
---
 fs/smb/server/auth.c | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/fs/smb/server/auth.c b/fs/smb/server/auth.c
index e85d7b0ded30..9844aaad7ab3 100644
--- a/fs/smb/server/auth.c
+++ b/fs/smb/server/auth.c
@@ -24,7 +24,6 @@
 
 #include <linux/fips.h>
 #include <crypto/arc4.h>
-#include <crypto/des.h>
 
 #include "server.h"
 #include "smb_common.h"
-- 
2.53.0

